<title>USA: BASKETBALL-SECOND PHASE GROUPS IN THE EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP.</title>
<headline>BASKETBALL-SECOND PHASE GROUPS IN THE EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP.</headline>
<dateline>GERONA, Spain 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Groups for the second phase</p>
<p>of the European basketball championships.</p>
<p>NB: Teams that have played each other in the first phase do</p>
<p>not play each other again. Four teams each from Group E and F</p>
<p>qualify for the quarter finals, with results from the first</p>
<p>phase also being used to determine classifications.</p>
<p>Group E (in Gerona):</p>
<p> Greece		    Lithuania</p>
<p> Russia		    Israel</p>
<p> Turkey		    France</p>
<p> (from Group A)	  (from Group B)</p>
<p>Group F (in Badalona):</p>
<p> Italy		     Spain</p>
<p> Yugoslavia		Croatia</p>
<p> Poland		    Germany</p>
<p> (group Group C)	 (from Group D)</p>
<p>Games to be played on 29th, 30th June, and 1st July.</p>
</text>
